Central QSR Agent[JC1.1]
Design Overview
Audience: Business Unit stakeholders & Principal Engineers    Status: Draft    Date: August 2026

1. Introduction
We are building a Central QSR Agent: a single reasoning agent that runs on one edge box, talks to a store operator in plain language, and acts on what is happening in the store without being asked. The agent does not contain any store logic itself. Instead, a set of services — some real Intel Retail Suite pipelines, some abstracting device categories, some simulated — each expose their data and actions to the agent through a uniform contract. The agent listens for what it cares about, reads history when it needs to compare, and calls tools to act.
Why it matters. Today's retail AI pipelines each do one job well but run in isolation — they detect and report, but they do not reason across one another or act on their own. The Central QSR Agent turns those separate pipelines into a single store that reasons and responds, on one Intel edge box, through one operator-facing assistant. It is designed so that real pipelines and simulated stand-ins are interchangeable, letting us demonstrate the full experience now and swap in production pipelines as they become available — with no change to the agent.

