3. What is EdgeMart[RB3.1][AP3.2][RB3.3][JC3.4]
EdgeMart (internal project name “pos_mcp_simulation”) is an existing in-house proof-of-concept: a self-contained point-of-sale demo for a café and grocery store, with a 3D visual store simulator, a backend, and an “agent chat” that answers questions by calling tools. It runs with no cameras and no special hardware.
EdgeMart proves the reactive slice of our vision — an operator can ask a question in plain language and the agent answers by calling tools — and it contains a full software simulator of a store's activity. It does not yet provide the autonomous, event-driven, and replayable behaviour the current requirement needs. It is therefore a valuable head-start for parts of this effort, but not the finished product (see Section 5).

4. Probable services and their capabilities
In the new design every capability — real or simulated — becomes a “service” that presents the same simple contract to the agent: what it can sense, what history it can report, and what actions (if any) it can take. Most vision pipelines are sensors (the agent reads and reacts); the actuators — the things the agent can actually change — are signage, boards, table state, inventory, and operator notifications.
