5. What we reuse from EdgeMart (and what we do not)
EdgeMart accelerates this effort, but only in part. The following makes explicit what carries forward and what has to be built fresh for the current requirement.
We reuse
Reused from EdgeMart	Why it carries forward
The store simulator (“sim stack”)	The software that generates realistic store activity — customers, tables, transactions, movement. These are exactly the capabilities that have no vision pipeline today (tables, drive-thru, inventory, footfall). This is EdgeMart's single biggest contribution.

We do NOT reuse (not what the current requirement needs)
Not reused	Why not
The point-of-sale user interface[RB9.1][AP9.2][RB9.3]	EdgeMart's UI is a cashier / checkout screen. The current requirement needs an operator decision interface — ask the agent, see alerts, and see what the agent did and why. That is a different, purpose-built surface, not a POS screen.
The agent chat integration as built	EdgeMart wires the agent for reactive question-and-answer only. The current requirement needs autonomous, event-driven behaviour — the agent acting on store events on its own. We keep the same agent framework, but replace this integration with the new event-driven design.[RB10.1][AP10.2]
The in-memory data store	EdgeMart holds simulated state in memory, so nothing can be replayed or measured. The new design gives every service a durable, replayable record — the foundation for later benchmarking.

6. How it fits together
Services report what happens to a common place the agent watches[JC11.1][AP11.2]. The agent reasons on a schedule, and reacts — asking a service for detail, comparing against history, and telling a service to act — all through the same simple contract. A store operator talks to the agent in plain language and sees what it did and why.
The one rule that makes this work: the agent cannot tell a simulated service from a real one. Both present the same contract and the same kind of data. Whether a capability runs on the edge box, on its own hardware, or is simulated is a deployment choice — never a change to the agent. This is what lets us demonstrate the full experience now and swap real pipelines in as they land.

